# memory-brain — append-only ledgers merge as unions, not conflicts.
#
# claims/ledger.jsonl (and any other jsonl ledger under memory/) is designed
# to be append-only + last-wins reduce (see ClaimStore.list()'s recordedAt-based
# order-independent reduce). Without this, a normal 3-way git merge inserts
# `<<<<<<<` conflict markers into the file; parseJsonlLenient() then silently
# treats every marker line as a corrupt line and drops it — a claim can vanish
# with no error. `merge=union` keeps both sides' lines instead of conflicting.
memory/**/*.jsonl merge=union
